WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:04.460
What happens to Zoro after Luffy becomes Pirate
King?

00:00:04.460 --> 00:00:09.640
Roronoa Zoro is the favorite Straw Hat for
tons of One Piece fans, and we just can’t

00:00:09.640 --> 00:00:14.810
wait to see him achieve his goal of becoming
the world’s strongest swordsman.

00:00:14.810 --> 00:00:20.810
But what waits for Zoro after he finally defeats
Dracule Mihawk?

00:00:20.810 --> 00:00:25.529
After the One Piece is found and the World
Government is taken down, what’s left for

00:00:25.529 --> 00:00:27.099
our favorite pirate crew?

00:00:27.099 --> 00:00:32.439
While the manga will eventually end, we readers
want to imagine the world and the characters

00:00:32.439 --> 00:00:35.649
in it living on beyond that final page.

00:00:35.649 --> 00:00:40.309
Will Oda give us an epilogue that gives us
a happily ever after for each of our Straw

00:00:40.309 --> 00:00:44.200
Hat pirates - or will there be a bittersweet
twist?

00:00:44.200 --> 00:00:48.179
That’s what we want to speculate on today.

00:00:48.179 --> 00:00:52.180
For some Straw Hats, it’s easy to imagine
what they’ll do in the future.

00:00:52.180 --> 00:00:58.160
There will always be hungry people, and Sanji
wlil always want to cook for them, most likely

00:00:58.160 --> 00:01:00.660
with tasty fish from the All Blue.

00:01:00.660 --> 00:01:04.729
Franky will never want to stop tinkering with
his machines and building bigger and better

00:01:04.729 --> 00:01:09.140
ships, even after the Thousand Sunny completes
its voyage around the world.

00:01:09.140 --> 00:01:14.140
And with his immortality, Soul King Brook
will probably give Keith Richards a run for

00:01:14.140 --> 00:01:17.170
his money when it comes to rockstar longevity.

00:01:17.170 --> 00:01:20.300
But today, we want to focus on Roronoa Zoro.

00:01:20.300 --> 00:01:23.579
Zoro’s goal is to become the strongest swordsman
in the world.

00:01:23.579 --> 00:01:29.340
By the end of the series, it’s extremely
likely that Zoro will achieve that goal by

00:01:29.340 --> 00:01:33.110
facing down his mentor, Dracule Mihawk, once
and for all.

00:01:33.110 --> 00:01:38.930
Unlike some of the other Straw Hat’s dreams,
his has a singular goal, and when it’s done

00:01:38.930 --> 00:01:39.930
it’s done.

00:01:39.930 --> 00:01:43.799
By defeating Mihawk, he will definitively
become the strongest swordsman.

00:01:43.799 --> 00:01:48.079
His goal will be completed, so what comes
next?

00:01:48.079 --> 00:01:53.259
Zoro’s entire existence is characterized
by his pursuit of strength.

00:01:53.259 --> 00:01:57.090
He’s constantly lifting giant weights and
practicing his swordsmanship.

00:01:57.090 --> 00:02:02.320
He’s always surpassing his limits by cutting
down stronger and stronger opponents.

00:02:02.320 --> 00:02:07.350
He started from almost nothing, getting completely
washed by Mihawk.

00:02:07.350 --> 00:02:13.290
But eventually, in his duel with Daz Bones,
Zoro learned how to cut steel (possibly tapping

00:02:13.290 --> 00:02:17.379
into haki long before we ever learned about
it properly in the series.

00:02:17.379 --> 00:02:20.819
And now, he’s tapped into even Conqueror’s
Haki.)

00:02:20.819 --> 00:02:27.230
In Wano, he’s managed to match the strength
of the legendary Kozuki Oden by cutting Kaidou’s

00:02:27.230 --> 00:02:31.700
nearly-invincible scales as well as learning
Kinemon’s technique for cutting through

00:02:31.700 --> 00:02:32.700
flames.

00:02:32.700 --> 00:02:37.730
Now, it’s looking like he’ll have to fight
an opponent he can’t even see as the Straw

00:02:37.730 --> 00:02:44.590
Hats face off against the Blackbeard Pirates,
as he’ll likely fight Shiryu of the Rain.

00:02:44.590 --> 00:02:51.400
And if a popular fan theory is correct, he
may even fight someone who inherits Jozu’s

00:02:51.400 --> 00:02:55.700
fruit, learning to cut the hardest substance
in the world: diamond.

00:02:55.700 --> 00:03:02.209
What does someone who pursues strength so
single-mindedly do after they finally become

00:03:02.209 --> 00:03:04.110
the strongest swordsman in the world?

00:03:04.110 --> 00:03:07.910
What else does Zoro have to strive for?

00:03:07.910 --> 00:03:11.250
Speaking of striving for a big goal, though,
make sure to hit that subscribe button.

00:03:11.250 --> 00:03:13.129
Right now I’m trying to make it so that
my subscriber count, converted into berries,

00:03:13.129 --> 00:03:14.250
will outweigh the bounty of the slimy and
terrible Trebol: the worst Don Quixote family

00:03:14.250 --> 00:03:15.250
member, and someone we can only topple with
your help.

00:03:15.250 --> 00:03:16.250
But now, back to Zoro.

00:03:16.250 --> 00:03:20.330
Thankfully, when it comes to predicting what
Zoro might do in the future, we’re not working

00:03:20.330 --> 00:03:21.890
totally blind here.

00:03:21.890 --> 00:03:29.050
Oda has actually given us a few hints to what
the future might look like for the Straw Hats.

00:03:29.050 --> 00:03:33.730
In the SBS sections of the manga volumes,
he’s actually provided some illustrations

00:03:33.730 --> 00:03:39.140
of what various Straw Hats would look like
at age 40 or 60, and he generously gave us

00:03:39.140 --> 00:03:41.900
both good timelines and bad timelines.

00:03:41.900 --> 00:03:46.200
If you haven’t checked out these drawings
in the recent SBSes, definitely do yourself

00:03:46.200 --> 00:03:48.090
a favor and give them a look!

00:03:48.090 --> 00:03:52.900
For the good timeline, Zoro ages very gracefully.

00:03:52.900 --> 00:03:58.400
Really, he hardly looks to have aged at all,
save for a few wrinkles here and there.

00:03:58.400 --> 00:04:03.709
With a nice comedic touch, Zoro at age 40
declares that he has mastered the four-sword

00:04:03.709 --> 00:04:08.110
style and at age 60, he’s even upgraded
to five-swords.

00:04:08.110 --> 00:04:14.140
I’m not even sure I want to know how he’s
holding those fourth and fifth swords, but

00:04:14.140 --> 00:04:16.260
feel free to leave your best guesses down
in the comments.

00:04:16.260 --> 00:04:21.870
This goes to show, though, that Zoro’s pursuit
of strength doesn’t have to end just because

00:04:21.870 --> 00:04:24.150
he’s the strongest swordsman in the world.

00:04:24.150 --> 00:04:29.860
Even if he overcomes Mihawk and stands above
any other challenger, there’s still one

00:04:29.860 --> 00:04:33.390
important opponent he’ll have: himself.

00:04:33.390 --> 00:04:38.830
He can always continue lifting his oversized
weights and surpassing his own limits.

00:04:38.830 --> 00:04:44.040
He’ll likely maintain his disciplined training
rather than resting on his laurels.

00:04:44.040 --> 00:04:49.120
After all, he’s already achieved so much
in the story and that hasn’t changed his

00:04:49.120 --> 00:04:52.620
razor sharp focus on improving himself.

00:04:52.620 --> 00:04:57.640
As we mentioned earlier, he learned how to
cut steel, but that’s only the beginning

00:04:57.640 --> 00:04:59.100
of what Zoro has accomplished.

00:04:59.100 --> 00:05:05.460
He’s helped hold his crew together in the
toughest moments, such as when Usopp left

00:05:05.460 --> 00:05:07.210
the Straw Hats during Water 7.

00:05:07.210 --> 00:05:12.760
He’s defeated formidable foes like the legendary
warrior from Wano, Ryuma, gaining the fabled

00:05:12.760 --> 00:05:14.110
sword Shusui.

00:05:14.110 --> 00:05:18.990
And also in Thriller Bark, who could forget
him taking on all of Luffy’s pain in order

00:05:18.990 --> 00:05:24.740
to save the rest of his crew, and in a truly
iconic moment, professing that “Nothing

00:05:24.740 --> 00:05:25.740
Happened.”

00:05:25.740 --> 00:05:31.240
And recently in Wano, like we mentioned, he’s
managed not only to scar Kaidou, a feat formerly

00:05:31.240 --> 00:05:38.480
only accomplished by Oden, but also to temporarily
block a dual attack from Kaidou and Big Mom.

00:05:38.480 --> 00:05:44.380
He also, of course, tamed Oden’s sword,
Enma and evidently even fought back the grim

00:05:44.380 --> 00:05:45.680
reaper himself.

00:05:45.680 --> 00:05:52.110
And as we enter the final saga, Zoro shows
no signs of slowing down.

00:05:52.110 --> 00:05:57.450
Like Mihawk, he may live a quiet and reserved
life, though with barrels of sake instead

00:05:57.450 --> 00:05:59.100
of glasses of wine.

00:05:59.100 --> 00:06:03.780
He’ll train consistently, waiting and searching
for the time that a worthy opponent may arise,

00:06:03.780 --> 00:06:09.250
wanting to take the mantle of world’s greatest
swordsman for themselves.

00:06:09.250 --> 00:06:16.950
However, on the opposite end of things, we
have the terrifying “bad timeline” Zoro.

00:06:16.950 --> 00:06:24.520
Tragically, he loses his hair along with several
teeth, and definitely stops working out.

00:06:24.520 --> 00:06:29.141
At age 40, he’s long given up swordsmanship,
claiming that “holding that katana with

00:06:29.141 --> 00:06:31.480
my mouth makes my back hurt.”

00:06:31.480 --> 00:06:38.290
If I were to guess, I’d say that’s probably
how he lost those teeth, too.

00:06:38.290 --> 00:06:43.720
At age 60, things are even worse - in this
timeline he’s become a beggar, claiming

00:06:43.720 --> 00:06:47.560
that he’ll bow down to anyone who will give
him some spare change.

00:06:47.560 --> 00:06:54.160
We can only guess as to what terrible events
would convince Zoro to drop his swordsmanship

00:06:54.160 --> 00:06:58.010
along with his convictions.

00:06:58.010 --> 00:07:03.850
The Zoro we know would never bow to anyone
- after all, he’s a conqueror, just like

00:07:03.850 --> 00:07:04.850
his captain.

00:07:04.850 --> 00:07:08.860
And while Oda’s drawings give us hints as
to what Zoro might do after the story, it

00:07:08.860 --> 00:07:11.900
doesn’t tell us where he’ll be doing it.

00:07:11.900 --> 00:07:16.850
Where might Zoro go after Luffy becomes the
pirate king and the Thousand Sunny stops its

00:07:16.850 --> 00:07:17.850
voyage?

00:07:17.850 --> 00:07:22.710
There are a few options - after Zoro dethrones
Mihawk, perhaps he’ll eventually take over

00:07:22.710 --> 00:07:27.630
as the steward of Kuraigana Island after the
Shichibukai passes on.

00:07:27.630 --> 00:07:30.570
Someone has to keep all those apes company,
after all.

00:07:30.570 --> 00:07:36.700
However, occupying Mihawk’s home chateau
seems more up Perona’s alley - and something

00:07:36.700 --> 00:07:40.780
tells me Zoro would rather not spend any extra
time with her.

00:07:40.780 --> 00:07:44.630
After all, he’s not as keen on that Tim
Burton, goth aesthetic.

00:07:44.630 --> 00:07:48.490
If any Straw Hat were to look at home there,
it’d probably be Brook.

00:07:48.490 --> 00:07:54.410
I could also see Zoro ending up on Sabaody
Archipelago, taking up Silvers Rayleigh’s

00:07:54.410 --> 00:07:55.410
job.

00:07:55.410 --> 00:07:58.680
Zoro’s the first mate to the future pirate
king, so maybe it would be fitting for him

00:07:58.680 --> 00:08:03.650
to follow in the footsteps of his predecessor,
the first mate of Gol D. Roger.

00:08:03.650 --> 00:08:08.630
Zoro, too, could keep an eye out for up and
coming rookies making their way to the New

00:08:08.630 --> 00:08:13.320
World, and perhaps even giving them a test
of strength before they descend into the second

00:08:13.320 --> 00:08:18.630
half of the Grand Line.

00:08:18.630 --> 00:08:27.470
Another option could be to return to Wano.

00:08:27.470 --> 00:08:32.320
After all, it’s become clear that Zoro is
a Shimotsuki, and even the possible heir to

00:08:32.320 --> 00:08:33.540
a Daimyo position.

00:08:33.540 --> 00:08:39.810
Zoro’s way around a katana, and the way
he seems to attract Wano blades like the Kitetsus,

00:08:39.810 --> 00:08:45.470
the Wado Ichimonji, Shusui, and now Enma to
him seem to suggest a natural attraction to

00:08:45.470 --> 00:08:46.470
his homeland.

00:08:46.470 --> 00:08:51.690
I’m sure certain shippers would not be disappointed
to see him end up with Hiyori either, given

00:08:51.690 --> 00:08:54.480
some of their chemistry in the Wano arc.

00:08:54.480 --> 00:09:00.000
Besides, where better to find tough opponents
than among the samurai of Wano.

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:03.940
Perhaps, though, Zoro will travel all the
way back to the East Blue, to his home in

00:09:03.940 --> 00:09:05.320
Shimotsuki Village.

00:09:05.320 --> 00:09:09.261
After becoming the greatest swordsman, he’ll
visit Kuina’s grave to show her that he

00:09:09.261 --> 00:09:14.750
achieved his goal - after all, he did it in
part to carry on her legacy.

00:09:14.750 --> 00:09:21.270
A truly touching scene could be him teaching
young pupils at the dojo where he learned

00:09:21.270 --> 00:09:26.370
swordsmanship, igniting the same spark in
them to become the strongest that was lit

00:09:26.370 --> 00:09:27.450
in him as a child.

00:09:27.450 --> 00:09:32.220
And since we already suggested that Zoro could
end up with Hiyroi, while we’re shipping,

00:09:32.220 --> 00:09:35.780
we might as well wonder if he might become
closer to Tashigi.

00:09:35.780 --> 00:09:40.980
Obviously their relationship has been pretty
strained, with him comparing her to Kuina,

00:09:40.980 --> 00:09:46.030
and her being a marine and trying to capture
his crew, but they sure do love a good sword,

00:09:46.030 --> 00:09:48.640
so that’s something they have in common.

00:09:48.640 --> 00:09:51.340
Maybe Zoro will never settle down at all.

00:09:51.340 --> 00:09:55.650
Something tells me Luffy will always be up
for an adventure, and he’ll probably need

00:09:55.650 --> 00:09:58.800
his most reliable crew mate at his side.

00:09:58.800 --> 00:10:04.920
And if you really want to understand why Zoro
is so loyal to Luffy and how their relationship

00:10:04.920 --> 00:10:10.570
has grown throughout the story, you simply
can’t miss out on that video right here.

